 oysters when comparing them to Acme and Felix's. Their crawfish bread was also delicious and was a carved out loaf of bread with a crawfish, sauce, cheese and bell peppers in it. It was definitely good like the Yelp reviews had mentioned and one do the reasons why we chose Mr Ed's. Service was great too and our server, Tam, was attentive and entertaining. Definitely a place we would return to during our next trip."},{"business_id":"EME5hqQLjBD7e2cLryupbA","review_id":"SR9f33USmj1KgHWv2TLOqA","date":"2016-09-08T23:36:27","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9510114192962646,"text_excerpt":"We enjoyed mr. Ed's that we actually ended up coming here twice. Our first stop was for lunch and for about 5 people we spend just over $150. It was a great deal considering we had 3 appetizers including black and grilled alligator, definitely get it this way instead of fried, calamari and a seafood bread. Don't skip out on the seafood bread just because it doesn't have a description. Between the Cajun sauce comma the Crawfish and everything else wonderful about it it was definitely crowd-pleaser and sizable enough for everyone to share. I can't quite remember what it was but you don't know what I'm talking about when you see it on the menu get the bread. The number one most important thi..."},{"business_id":"EME5hqQLjBD7e2cLryupbA","review_id":"Cyr56mkIK5hFkXC8Il_JZg","date":"2019-03-08T03:52:19","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9442138075828552,"text_excerpt":"The oysters here are amazing . We ordered a dozen of all three raw charbroiled and jalapeño charbroiled. The food is on point but the servers were a little slow and ours was hard of hearing I think. Otherwise I plan on being back for sure definitely a top contender for oysters in New Orleans"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"EME5hqQLjBD7e2cLryupbA","photo_id":"4vWv4E5eb3VT_24a1wCobg","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/4vWv4E5eb3VT_24a1wCobg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9158614277839661},{"business_id":"EME5hqQLjBD